
== 0.1 + 0.2 ==
number: 0.1 + 0.2                  0.30000000000000004
number: 0.1 + 0.2 == 0.3           false
decimal: 0.1d + 0.2d               0.3
decimal: 0.1d + 0.2d == 0.3d       true

== adding 0.1 ten times ==
number sum                         0.99999999999999989
number sum == 1                    false
decimal sum                        1.0
decimal sum == 1d                  true

== adding one cent a thousand times ==
number total                       9.9999999999998312
number total == 10                 false
decimal total                      10.00
decimal total == 10d               true

== multiplication ==
number: 0.1 * 3                    0.30000000000000004
decimal: 0.1d * 3d                 0.3
number: 1.15 * 100                 114.99999999999999
decimal: 1.15d * 100d              115.00
number: 4.35 * 100                 434.99999999999994
decimal: 4.35d * 100d              435.00

== comparison ==
number: 0.1 + 0.7 < 0.8            true
decimal: 0.1d + 0.7d < 0.8d        false
number: 1.1 + 2.2 > 3.3            true
decimal: 1.1d + 2.2d > 3.3d        false

== rounding a half ==
number: string.format('%.2f', 2.675) 2.67
number 2.675 stored as             2.6749999999999998
decimal: round(2.675d, 2)          2.68
decimal: round(2.675d, 2, 'awayfromzero') 2.68
decimal: round(2.665d, 2) half-even 2.66
decimal: round(2.665d, 2, 'awayfromzero') 2.67

== where decimals do NOT help ==
1d / 3d (finite digits)            0.333333333333333333333333333
1d / 3d * 3d                       0.999999999999999999999999999
(1d / 3d) * 3d == 1d               false
1d / 3d is not exact either        false

== converting from a double keeps the shortest digits ==
decimal.create(0.1)                0.1
decimal.create(0.1 + 0.2)          0.30000000000000004
decimal.create(2.675)              2.675
decimal.create(1/3)                0.3333333333333333
